            "type": "text",
            "text": "Invite\nToday\nYou said\nCannot reach RealAI backend. Tried: file:///health. Start the server (realai_server.py) and ensure PORT=8000 is bound.\nCopilot said\nYou’re looking at the Fusion UI, and it’s telling you exactly what’s wrong:\n“Cannot reach RealAI backend.”    “Tried: file:///health.”    “Start the server (realai_server.py) and ensure PORT=8000 is bound.”\nThat UI is only a frontend. It cannot function until the backend API server is actually running and listening on localhost:8000.\nLet’s fix this cleanly and quickly.\n✅ Why file:///health fails\nThe Fusion UI is trying to reach the backend’s health endpoint:\nCode\nCopy\nhttp://localhost:8000/health \nBut since the backend isn’t running, the UI falls back to a file:// URL, which will never work. That’s why you see:\n“Tried: file:///health.”\n✅ Start the backend correctly (Windows, your repo layout)\n1. Go to your RealAI project root\nCode\nCopy\ncd C:\\Users\\tsmit\\realai \n2. Run the backend module\nTry this first:\nCode\nCopy\npython -m realai.api_server --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 \nIf your repo uses the older layout:\nCode\nCopy\npython realai_server.py \nor:\nCode\nCopy\npython -m server.app \n(You’ve used this one before successfully.)\n3. Confirm it actually bound to port 8000\nIn a second PowerShell window:\nCode\nCopy\ncurl http://localhost:8000/health \nYou should get JSON like:\nCode\nCopy\n{\"status\":\"healthy\",\"model\":\"realai-2.0\"} \nIf you get connection refused → the server didn’t bind to 8000.\n⚠️ Important: Your RealAI sometimes binds to 8000 even when you specify 8080\nYou’ve seen this before. So after starting the server, always check the console output:\nCode\nCopy\nServer running at http://0.0.0.0:8000 \nIf it prints 8000, the UI will work. If it prints anything else, the Fusion UI won’t connect.\n🔧 If the server fails to import RealAI\nYou previously saw:\nCode\nCopy\nImportError: cannot import name 'RealAI' from 'realai' \nThat means your realai folder structure has multiple versions or conflicting modules. If that happens again, tell me the exact error text and I’ll fix the module path.\n⭐ Ready to continue\nIf you want, I can walk you through this step-by-step in real time until the backend is reachable.\nJust say:\n“Start from step 1.”\nEdit in a page\nYou said\n\"\"\"RealAI Unified Server - Fusion UI as Default Run with: python realai_server.py \"\"\"  import os  print(\"=== RealAI Unified Server (Fusion UI Priority) ===\")  try:     from realai.api_server import run_server     print(\"✓ Loaded api_server\")      # DevMode     try:         from core.devmode import devmode         devmode.enable(\"AtomicFizz\")         print(\"✓ DevMode enabled\")     except Exception:         pass      host = os.environ.get(\"HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\")     port = int(os.environ.get(\"PORT\", \"8000\"))      # Ensure local defaults are unified: bind to 127.0.0.1 unless explicitly overridden.     # (Avoid surprises where HOST=0.0.0.0 causes UI origin/port inference issues.)     host = os.environ.get(\"HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\")      # Force Fusion UI as the main interface (api_server is expected to honor these env vars)     os.environ.setdefault(\"REALAI_UI_PATH\", \"fusion-ui\")     os.environ.setdefault(\"REALAI_SKIP_AUTH\", \"true\")     os.environ.setdefault(\"REALAI_DEFAULT_UI\", \"fusion\")      print(f\"Server running at http://{host}:{port}\")     print(f\"→ Fusion UI: http://{host}:{port}/\")     print(f\"→ Health: http://{host}:{port}/health\")      run_server(host=host, port=port)  except Exception as e:     print(f\"Error: {e}\")     import traceback     traceback.print_exc()\nCopilot said\nYour realai_server.py is correct, but your Fusion UI tab shows no backend reachable, meaning the server either:\nnever actually started,\ncrashed on import,\nor bound to the wrong interface/port.\nLet’s walk through what your script should do and why your UI is falling back to file:///health.\n🎯 What your script is supposed to do\nYour script prints:\nCode\nCopy\nServer running at http://127.0.0.1:8000 → Fusion UI: http://127.0.0.1:8000/ → Health: http://127.0.0.1:8000/health \nThen it calls:\npython\nCopy\nrun_server(host=host, port=port) \nIf everything loads correctly, the Fusion UI should immediately connect to:\nCode\nCopy\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8000/health \nBut your UI shows:\nCannot reach RealAI backend   Tried: file:///health\nThis only happens when the backend never bound to 8000.\n🔥 The most likely failure point\nYour script tries:\npython\nCopy\nfrom realai.api_server import run_server \nIf this import fails, your server never starts.\nYour UI tab confirms this: The backend is not running at all.\n🧪 Step-by-step fix (do this now)\n1. Run the unified server directly\nOpen PowerShell:\nCode\nCopy\ncd C:\\Users\\tsmit\\realai python realai_server.py \nWatch the console carefully.\nYou should see:\nCode\nCopy\n✓ Loaded api_server ✓ DevMode enabled Server running at http://127.0.0.1:8000 → Fusion UI: http://127.0.0.1:8000/ → Health: http://127.0.0.1:8000/health \nIf you do NOT see “Loaded api_server”, the import failed.\nTell me the error text and I’ll fix it.\n2. Verify the backend is actually listening\nIn a second PowerShell window:\nCode\nCopy\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health \nExpected:\nCode\nCopy\n{\"status\":\"healthy\"} \nIf you get:\nconnection refused\ntimeout\n404 from file:///health\n→ backend never started.\n3. Confirm the host binding\nYour script forces:\npython\nCopy\nhost = os.environ.get(\"HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\") \nThis is good — Fusion UI expects 127.0.0.1, not 0.0.0.0.\nBut if your environment has:\nCode\nCopy\nPORT=8080 \nyour script will still print:\nCode\nCopy\nServer running at http://127.0.0.1:8000 \nbecause you default to 8000.\nSo the UI will always try 8000.\nIf the backend actually bound to 8080, the UI will fail.\n🧩 Your next move\nRun:\nCode\nCopy\npython realai_server.py \nand paste the full console output here.\nI’ll diagnose the exact failure and fix it cleanly.\nYou’re very close — the UI is fine, the backend just isn’t alive.\nEdit in a page\nMessage Copilot"
